tags: descendant-depth

A limit of the node: the most levels of descendants below one account.

The value is an integer in levels. Example: 8. The node refuses a start that makes a deeper descendant.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=descendant-depth
per=one account
rule=The node refuses a start that makes a deeper descendant.
scope=none
unit=levels
